{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidGroupNStrand"],"declarations":89,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStarts_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStarts_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":932,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L932-L947","doc":"**No strand is walked twice.** Nodup within each component\n(`walk_nodup`) and disjointness across components\n(`walk_disjoint_of_ne_leader`), combined over the concatenation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapsOf_eq_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapsOf_eq_map","kind":"theorem","line":925,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L925-L929","doc":"The laps are exactly the laps of the starting positions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStarts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStarts","kind":"def","line":919,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L919-L922","doc":"The starting positions of the laps, in traversal order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":879,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L879-L916","doc":"**A component walk does not repeat.** The orbit is traversed exactly once,\nso the walk visits each strand of its component a single time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.cycleLen_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.cycleLen_inv","kind":"theorem","line":870,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L870-L875","doc":"**Inverting a permutation does not change any cycle's length.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_disjoint_of_ne_leader","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_disjoint_of_ne_leader","kind":"theorem","line":832,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L832-L843","doc":"**Walks from distinct leaders never meet.** Different components are\ndisjoint, so no strand is walked twice.\n\nStated in a *single* permutation: after the `stepPerm` refactor the walk and the\nleadership are both taken in the same permutation, so the earlier\n`sameCycle_inv` reconciliation between `f` and `f⁻¹` is no longer needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapsOf_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapsOf_length","kind":"theorem","line":821,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L821-L829","doc":"**One lap per strand: the traversal takes exactly `n` laps.**\n\nThe List/Finset step is definitional — for `Fin n` a `Finset.sum` over a\nfiltered `univ` and a `List.sum` over a filtered `finRange` are the *same term*,\nso no transfer lemma is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.sum_cycleLen_leaders","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.sum_cycleLen_leaders","kind":"theorem","line":801,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L801-L818","doc":"**The partition fact.** The components cover `Fin n` exactly: summing each\nleader's component size gives `n`. Proved by counting the fibres of `leaderOf`,\nwhich `card_fiber_leader` identifies with the components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.card_fiber_leader","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.card_fiber_leader","kind":"theorem","line":764,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L764-L798","doc":"**A leader's fibre is its component, and its size is `cycleLen`.** The two\ncases are the two shapes a component can have: a lone fixed strand, or a genuine\ncycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf_of_isLeader","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf_of_isLeader","kind":"theorem","line":758,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L758-L761","doc":"A leader is its own leader. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":746,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L746-L755","doc":"**Two positions share a leader exactly when they share a cycle** — so the\nfibres of `leaderOf` are precisely the components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf_sameCycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf_sameCycle","kind":"theorem","line":742,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L742-L743","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf_isLeader","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf_isLeader","kind":"theorem","line":738,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L738-L739","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leaderOf","kind":"def","line":733,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L733-L735","doc":"The leader of `p`'s component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.cycleLen_eq_card_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.cycleLen_eq_card_support","kind":"theorem","line":720,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L720-L724","doc":"**Otherwise `cycleLen` is exactly the size of the component.** So the walk\ntakes one lap per strand of the component — no more, no fewer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.cycleLen_of_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.cycleLen_of_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":713,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L713-L718","doc":"A strand that closes up alone needs one lap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.descending_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.descending_nil","kind":"theorem","line":700,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L700-L704","doc":"The identity braid is descending — vacuously, having no crossings. Recorded\nbecause it is the base of the reduction: every word reduces to a descending one,\nand this is the extreme case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.Descending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.Descending","kind":"def","line":691,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L691-L698","doc":"**Descending**: every crossing is *first met as an over-crossing*.\n\nThis is the hypothesis the MFW base case is about, and it is now a definition\nrather than a research question: `verdictsFor` is well posed because the\ntraversal is ordered (`exists_leader` + `leader_unique`) and because each\ncrossing contributes exactly two entries (`card_involved`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.verdictsFor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.verdictsFor","kind":"def","line":684,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L684-L688","doc":"The verdicts recorded for crossing `k`, in traversal order — the `k`-th\ncolumn of the laps, with the strands not involved dropped. By `card_involved`\nthis list has exactly two entries: one `over` and one `under`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.length_of_mem_lapsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.length_of_mem_lapsOf","kind":"theorem","line":674,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L674-L681","doc":"**Every lap has one slot per crossing.** This is what makes the `k`-th\ncolumn well defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.traversalVerdicts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.traversalVerdicts","kind":"def","line":670,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L670-L672","doc":"The full traversal, flattened. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapsOf","kind":"def","line":657,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L657-L667","doc":"The traversal as a **list of laps**, in order: every component (by\nincreasing least position), each walked once, one entry per lap.\n\nKept as a list-of-laps rather than pre-flattened because every lap has the same\nlength — one slot per crossing — so crossing `k`'s verdicts are the `k`-th\ncolumn. Flattening first would turn that projection into modular arithmetic on a\nglobal index for no gain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepPerm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepPerm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":653,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L653-L654","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepPerm","kind":"def","line":640,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L640-L651","doc":"**The lap-step permutation**: where one full pass through the word sends a\nstrand. By `lapStep_eq` this is `(closurePerm w)⁻¹`, and it — not `closurePerm`\n— is the permutation the traversal actually walks.\n\nNaming it matters beyond taste. Stating the walk under `(closurePerm w)⁻¹` while\ncounting laps with `cycleLen (closurePerm w)` forced a `cycleLen f⁻¹ p =\ncycleLen f p` bridge across a `DecidableRel` instance divergence. That bridge is\nnow proved (`cycleLen_inv`, below), but phrasing every part of the traversal in\nthe *same* permutation is still the better fix: it removes the need for the\nbridge rather than paying for it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leader_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.leader_unique","kind":"theorem","line":633,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L633-L638","doc":"**Uniqueness**: a cycle has exactly one leader, so no component is walked\ntwice. Together with `exists_leader` this is what the mutable `seen_start` set\nwas doing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.exists_leader","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.exists_leader","kind":"theorem","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L615-L630","doc":"**Every position has a leader in its own cycle** — so every component is\nreached by the traversal, none is skipped. The least element of a nonempty\nfinite set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.IsLeader","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.IsLeader","kind":"def","line":610,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L610-L612","doc":"`p` starts a component: it is the least position in its own cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walkVerdicts_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walkVerdicts_length","kind":"theorem","line":592,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L592-L597","doc":"**`k` laps of `m` crossings each.** The encounter count is exactly what it\nshould be, which is the arithmetic the global ordering will rest on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walkVerdicts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walkVerdicts","kind":"def","line":587,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L587-L590","doc":"The verdicts collected while walking a component: one lap per position\nvisited, concatenated in visit order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_sameCycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_sameCycle","kind":"theorem","line":579,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L579-L585","doc":"Every position on the walk lies in the same cycle as the start — the walk\nstays inside its component, which is what makes it a *component* walk. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_zero","kind":"theorem","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L576-L577","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk_length","kind":"theorem","line":572,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L572-L574","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.walk","kind":"def","line":568,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L568-L570","doc":"The positions visited in the first `k` laps from `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.pow_cycleLen_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.pow_cycleLen_apply","kind":"theorem","line":561,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L561-L566","doc":"**The walk closes up.** After `cycleLen` laps the strand is back where it\nstarted — so the component walk is well posed without a termination argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.cycleLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.cycleLen","kind":"def","line":556,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L556-L559","doc":"The number of laps that returns a strand to its start: the length of its\ncycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep_flipSign_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep_flipSign_cons","kind":"theorem","line":537,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L537-L542","doc":"Switching a crossing leaves the lap's *itinerary* untouched and flips\nexactly the verdicts — the lap-level form of `closurePerm_switch` together with\n`stepOver_flipSign`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep_eq_self_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep_eq_self_iff","kind":"theorem","line":523,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L523-L535","doc":"Hence a lap returns to its start exactly on the fixed points of the closure\npermutation — the strands that close up alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep_eq","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L513-L521","doc":"**A lap is the inverse of `closurePerm`.** The lap applies the first letter\nfirst; `closurePerm`, being a product, applies the last letter first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapVerdicts_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapVerdicts_length","kind":"theorem","line":504,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L504-L511","doc":"**One verdict slot per crossing** — so the crossing index really is the list\nindex, which is what makes \"the first crossing met as an under-crossing\"\nexpressible without separate bookkeeping. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapVerdicts_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapVerdicts_nil","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L501-L502","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep_nil","kind":"theorem","line":499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L499-L499","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapVerdicts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapVerdicts","kind":"def","line":493,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L493-L497","doc":"What a strand at position `p` meets during one full pass: one entry per\ncrossing, in word order. `none` = not involved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.lapStep","kind":"def","line":488,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L488-L491","doc":"Where a strand at position `p` ends up after one full pass through `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_flipSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_flipSign","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L460-L470","doc":"Switching a crossing flips both verdicts — the over/under counterpart of\n`closurePerm_switch`, which said the *positions* are untouched. Together: a\ncrossing change is exactly an exchange of over for under. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_isSome_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_isSome_iff","kind":"theorem","line":444,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L444-L458","doc":"**A strand is involved in a crossing exactly when the crossing moves it.**\nThis is what ties the over/under data to `closurePerm`: the traversal records an\nencounter precisely at the positions the permutation does not fix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_lo_ne_hi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_lo_ne_hi","kind":"theorem","line":437,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L437-L442","doc":"**The two strands of a crossing get opposite verdicts.** One passes over,\nthe other under — the defining property of a crossing, and the reason each\ncrossing contributes exactly one `over` and one `under` to the traversal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_hi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_hi","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L433-L435","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_lo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver_lo","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L429-L431","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.stepOver","kind":"def","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L422-L427","doc":"Which strand passes over, as seen from position `p`. `none` when `p` is not\none of the two strands involved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L401-L407","doc":"**The reference engine's component count agrees with `components`.** Its\nstrand map is the inverse of `closurePerm`, and inversion preserves cycle type\nand support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L390-L399","doc":"Reversing a braid word inverts its closure permutation. Each crossing is an\ninvolution, so reversal is exactly inversion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.length_eq_of_gens_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.length_eq_of_gens_eq","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L365-L371","doc":"Length is likewise a function of the generator sequence — recorded because\nthe reduction needs `n`, `c` **and** the crossing count to be preserved, leaving\n`e` as the only quantity that moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_eq_of_gens_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_eq_of_gens_eq","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L359-L363","doc":"**`c` is blind to every crossing sign at once.** This is what the reduction\nto a descending word preserves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_eq_of_gens_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_eq_of_gens_eq","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L344-L357","doc":"**Two braid words with the same generator sequence have the same closure\npermutation**, whatever their signs — so they close to the same number of\ncomponents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.gens_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.gens_cons","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L341-L342","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.gens_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.gens_nil","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L339-L339","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.gens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.gens","kind":"def","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L336-L337","doc":"The generator sequence of a braid word, forgetting all signs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_parity","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L308-L321","doc":"**The parity constraint, in the form the MFW window uses.** `e` and `n - c`\nalways share a parity — so `|e| ≤ n - c` is a same-parity, smaller-magnitude\nstatement, and the tightness the base-case measurement found at `|e| = n - c` is\nthe case where the parities coincide and nothing further is available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.n_sub_components","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.n_sub_components","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L298-L306","doc":"`n - c` counted the way the cycle data sees it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_le","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L291-L296","doc":"A braid closure has at most `n` components — one per strand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.card_support_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.card_support_le","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L288-L289","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.card_cycleType_le_card_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.card_cycleType_le_card_support","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L283-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.two_mul_card_cycleType_le_card_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.two_mul_card_cycleType_le_card_support","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L273-L281","doc":"**Every cycle costs at least two points**, so twice the number of nontrivial\ncycles fits inside the support. Stronger than the `card ≤ card` needed below,\nand not in Mathlib. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_parity_cycleType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_parity_cycleType","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L245-L263","doc":"**The writhe's parity is fixed by the closure permutation's cycle data.**\n\nThis is the parity constraint that makes `|e| ≤ n - c` a *same-parity, smaller\nmagnitude* statement rather than a bare inequality — the structure the base-case\nmeasurement found (tight exactly when the parities allow) and which no argument\nin the corpus had yet supplied. Stated against `cycleType` rather than `n - c`\nto avoid truncated `ℕ` subtraction; see the note below for what that costs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_sub_length_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_sub_length_even","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L223-L234","doc":"**The writhe has the parity of the crossing count** — each crossing\ncontributes `±1`, and both are odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.length_parity_cycleType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.length_parity_cycleType","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L213-L221","doc":"The crossing count and the cycle data agree in parity — the sign identity\nread through `Equiv.Perm.sign_of_cycleType`. Since `cycleType.sum` is the\nsupport size and `cycleType.card` the number of nontrivial cycles, this is the\nparity half of \"one transposition changes the orbit count by one\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.sign_closurePerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.sign_closurePerm","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L200-L211","doc":"**The closure permutation's sign is `(-1)` to the crossing count.** Each\ncrossing is one transposition, whatever its sign — the same sign-blindness that\nmakes `c` invariant under switching. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_smooth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_smooth","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L185-L191","doc":"**Smoothing moves the writhe by exactly 1** — the `e ↦ e - 1` of\n`mfw_step`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_smooth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_smooth","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L177-L183","doc":"**Smoothing removes the crossing**, so the permutation loses exactly that\ntransposition. Since multiplying by a transposition changes the orbit count by\none, this is where `c` moves — the other half of the skein step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_switch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_switch","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L169-L175","doc":"**Switching moves the writhe by exactly 2**, in the direction set by the\ncrossing's original sign — the `e ↦ e - 2` of `mfw_step`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_switch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_switch","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L165-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_switch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_switch","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L158-L163","doc":"**Switching a crossing does not move the permutation** — hence not `c`\neither. This is the half of the skein step that makes the induction work: `e`\nmoves while `c` and `n` stay put, so the window slides without changing width. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.crossingSwap_flipSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.crossingSwap_flipSign","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L155-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.flipSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.flipSign","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L151-L153","doc":"Flip a crossing's sign — the skein \"switch\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_two_two_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_two_two_crossings","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L129-L142","doc":"Two crossings on two strands cancel in the *permutation* (though not in the\nwrithe), so the closure has two components again — the 2-component unlink.\nTogether with the previous lemma this shows `components` tracks the parity of\nthe crossing count, as it must. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_two_one_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_two_one_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L118-L127","doc":"**One crossing on two strands closes to the unknot: `c = 1`, not 2.** The\ntwo strands are joined into a single circle. This is the smallest case where\n`components` could have been off by one, and it is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_two","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L107-L116","doc":"On two strands there is only one generator, so any crossing swaps `0` and\n`1`. (`Fin (2 - 1)` needs the subtraction reduced by hand — instance search will\nnot find `Subsingleton` through it.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.descendingWrithe_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.descendingWrithe_nil","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L91-L100","doc":"**The base corner, connected.** For the empty word the writhe is `0` and the\ncomponent count is `n`, so `MFWSkeinInduction.DescendingWrithe n c e` holds with\n`c = n`, `e = 0` — matching `descending_trivial_perm_writhe_zero`, which\npreviously had no braid word to be about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components_nil","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L86-L89","doc":"The identity braid closes to `n` disjoint circles — the `n`-component\nunlink. This is the `c = n` corner the window arithmetic pins down. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.components","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L80-L84","doc":"**The number of closure components.** Orbits of `closurePerm`: each\nnontrivial cycle is one component, and each fixed point is a component of its\nown (a strand that closes up alone). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.writhe_append","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L72-L78","doc":"The writhe is additive over concatenation — the other half of what the\nskein induction needs, since stacking braids adds their crossing signs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_append","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L66-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_cons","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L63-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm_nil","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.closurePerm","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L55-L59","doc":"The permutation of strand endpoints induced by a braid word. Its orbits are\nthe components of the Markov closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.crossingSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.crossingSwap","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L45-L53","doc":"The transposition a crossing induces on strand positions.\n\n**The sign is irrelevant here** — `σ_i` and `σ_i⁻¹` cross the same two strands\nand so induce the same permutation. That is why the closure component count `c`\nis insensitive to crossing changes, which is exactly what makes it a usable\ninvariant in the skein induction: switching a crossing moves `e` but fixes `c`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.loIdx_ne_hiIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.loIdx_ne_hiIdx","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L42-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.hiIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.hiIdx","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L39-L40","doc":"The upper of the two strand positions a generator `σ_i` acts on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.loIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BraidClosure.loIdx","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BraidClosure.lean#L36-L37","doc":"The lower of the two strand positions a generator `σ_i` acts on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}